Gotta love wands of wishing.

I started off as usual, Dwarvern Lawful Valkyrie. Hit level 5, went to
get Exie, and surprise surprise. "For what do you wish?" Luck was on
my side.

"A - a blessed +2 silver dragon scale mail"

Continuing on, I paced myself. I decided to do Soko first, needing to
polymorph two of the boulders before level 4. You know how items
appear on the pits that you need to put boulders in? I saw a /, and
grabbed it (it was right next to the last pit, so it wasn't actually
over one).

"r - a maple wand"

Engrave-testing it, I once again encountered the fateful message. Some
careful planning yielded five wishes from the wand in total (including
the wrest):

2 blessed scrolls of charging
a blessed greased +2 cloak of magic resistance
a blessed greased bag of holding
the blessed +2 Grayswandir
a blessed amulet of life saving

Yes, that was _one_ artifact there. Not five, one. I do listen to you
people :D

Continuing on, a wand of fire proved useful in the Soko zoo ("The
<monster> turns to flee!" x 50). The amulet of reflection was kind of
useless, but it's still worth a bit of gold.

I'm in the mines at the moment, just sorting out the shops. I think
I'll grab the gems, quarter their weight and then continue on to the
Quest.

Thoughts? Comments? I'm glad to hear it.

